{"id":"000W6H","title":"Sujiken Killer Sudoku","author":"ekeilty","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-22T22:29:51+00:00","posted":"Heute, 22:01 Uhr","rules":"Rules:\n\n• The grid consists of 45 cells, each filled with digits from 1 to 9. Digits cannot repeat in any row, column, or box.\n\n• Diagonal (Bishop's Move) Constraint: Digits cannot repeat along any diagonal in any direction. This means column 1, row 9, and the main diagonal are each sets of the digits 1 to 9.\n\n• Killer Cages: Digits inside each dashed cage must sum to the indicated cage total. No digit may repeat within a cage.\n\n• White Kropki Dots: Digits connected by a white dot must be consecutive.\n\nSolve on f-puzzles\n\nPersonal Comments:\n\nI don't think I squeezed everything I could out of this puzzle. There were a lot of very interesting constraints, but I often couldn't find a human-solvable path through them.\n\nIf any other (more experienced) setter wants to improve this puzzle, please feel free :)","solutionCode":"Column 1 + the main diagonal","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://tinyurl.com/5n6pdpxd","kind":"short"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://f-puzzles.com/?","linkKind":"short","summary":{"format":"fpuzzles","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":4,"hasSolution":false,"features":["killercage","difference"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-22T22:29:51+00:00"}